21:31.500 --> 21:33.440
It throws away a massive amount of data.

21:34.400 --> 21:36.740
But, and this is the genius of the architecture,

21:37.500 --> 21:40.080
if the model maintains high-reachability fidelity,

21:40.720 --> 21:44.820
the CLIO projection preserves the relative topological distances.

21:44.820 --> 21:47.240
So even if the map is vastly simplified,

21:47.960 --> 21:52.580
the distance between the financial bank and the river bank remains proportionally correct.

21:52.820 --> 21:53.260
Exactly.

21:53.420 --> 21:57.460
It preserves the shape of the labyrinth, even if it blurs the texture of the walls.

21:57.460 --> 21:59.180
That's a beautiful way to phrase it.

21:59.640 --> 22:03.880
The residual stream literally functions as a learned compressed coordinate system

22:03.880 --> 22:05.860
for the geometry of the deep future.

22:06.060 --> 22:06.280
Okay.

