24:13.620 --> 24:15.320
You undergo epistemic hysteresis.

24:15.860 --> 24:19.480
You permanently lose the belief state where you trusted them.

24:19.760 --> 24:24.560
You can't just forget the betrayal and return to the original coordinate on your mental map.

24:24.620 --> 24:24.920
Right.

24:25.100 --> 24:26.240
You can't unknow it.

24:26.240 --> 24:30.120
The geometry of a relationship's future is irreversibly contracted.

24:30.120 --> 24:35.720
That is a very human analog, but geometrically, it is exactly what happens to the neural network.

24:36.240 --> 24:41.400
Infliction explicitly connects this mathematical failure of the manifold to Goodhart's law.

24:41.620 --> 24:43.600
We all know Goodhart's law from economics, right?

24:43.600 --> 24:46.780
When a measure becomes a target, it ceases to be a good measure.

24:46.780 --> 24:53.740
If you reward a factory for the number of nails they produce, they will produce millions of tiny, useless nails.

24:54.300 --> 24:59.840
But the paper takes this economic adage and explains it purely through geometric contraction.

24:59.840 --> 25:06.840
If we subject an AI model to Goodhart Jamix, we are forcing it to geometrically collapse.

25:07.000 --> 25:08.160
Walk me through that collapse.

