If I force the AI to only care about maximizing a single metric, like what physically happens to its map.

25:16.340 --> 25:28.940
Well, when a system is heavily optimized for a single target metric, it begins dedicating all of its representational capacity, its entire high-dimensional vector space, to tracking the gradients of that one specific dimension.

25:28.940 --> 25:30.860
Because that's all it gets rewarded for.

25:30.920 --> 25:39.760
Right. And in doing so, to save, compute, and maximize the reward, it systematically discards all information about the perpendicular directions on the belief manifold.

25:40.060 --> 25:43.300
It throws away the rest of the map just to sprint as fast as it can in one direction.

25:43.440 --> 25:48.460
Yes. Its massive, multidimensional reachability cone drastically contracts.

25:48.760 --> 25:51.540
It flattens into a single line and eventually collapses to a point.

25:51.740 --> 25:52.400
That's terrifying.

25:52.400 --> 25:56.880
The system suffers profound, progressive, epistemic hysteresis.

25:56.880 --> 26:05.980
Yes. It forecloses all the latent distinctions it would actually need to realize that its target metric has completely diverged from underlying reality.

26:06.280 --> 26:09.880
This raises an important question. Wait, I stole your catchphrase.

